---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import Grid from '@components/Grid.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Agency Gone Quiet or Not Delivering?"
  description="Has your digital agency gone quiet or not delivering? Get a clear, honest plan within 48 hours. No lock-in contracts, Australian-owned team that gets it done."
>
  <section id="hero">
    <Grid>
      <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2 lg:col-span-5">
        <h1>Agency Gone Quiet or Not Delivering?</h1>
        <p>Get a clear, honest plan within 48 hours. No lock-in contracts, no jargon, just a straight answer.</p>
        <!-- CTA goes here: Book a free call -->
      </div>
    </Grid>
  </section>

  <section id="scenario">
    <Grid>
      <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2">
        <article>
          <h3>Your agency has gone quiet or shut down?</h3>
          <p>We can get your site secured and back under your control within days, not weeks.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Your agency is slow to respond or not delivering?</h3>
          <p>You shouldn't have to chase your own website. We'll take it from here.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>You're just not happy with the results or the cost anymore</h3>
          <p>A second opinion costs nothing, and there's no pressure either way.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </Grid>
  </section>

  <section id="about-us">
    <Grid>
      <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2">
        <h2>Why us?</h2>
        <p>
          We have been through this before. Pixel Agency was founded by people who helped a previous agency's clients
          move their sites to safety when that agency closed without warning. We know what this feels like from the
          other side.
        </p>
        <p>
          We've seen agency relationships go wrong in pretty much every way they can go wrong, from an agency vanishing
          overnight with no warning, to a slow decline in quality nobody wants to admit is happening. Either way, the
          fix starts the same: understanding exactly what you have, and what you're missing.
        </p>
        <!-- Place testimonials here -->
      </div>
    </Grid>
  </section>

  <section id="what-happens-next">
    <Grid>
      <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2">
        <h2>What happens next?</h2>

        <article>
          <strong>1.</strong>
          <h3>Free call</h3>
          <p>We listen to what's actually happened, no obligation.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <strong>2.</strong>
          <h3>Review</h3>
          <p>We check what you currently have access to and what state things are in.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <strong>3.</strong>
          <h3>Clear written plan</h3>
          <p>A straightforward summary of options and cost.</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <strong>4.</strong>
          <h3>Deliver</h3>
          <p>We implement the agreed plan and ensure your site is secure and running smoothly.</p>
        </article>

        <!-- CTA goes here: Book a free call -->
      </div>
    </Grid>

    <section id="checklist">
      <Grid>
        <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2">
          <h2>Not ready to talk yet?</h2>
          <p>
            Whatever happens with your current agency, there are five things every business should control outright.
            Answer honestly, most people are surprised by what they don't actually have. We also have a more in-depth
            article on
            <a href="/insights/how-to-protect-your-business-in-case-your-agency-closes"
              >how to protect your business in case your agency closes</a
            >.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Do you own your domain name outright, registered to your business, not your agency?</li>
            <li>Do you have direct login access to your hosting account?</li>
            <li>Do you have admin access to your website's CMS?</li>
            <li>Do you have access to your website's source code, or a current backup of it?</li>
            <li>
              Is your business email independent of your website hosting, so it keeps working even if your site goes
              down?
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            If you answered yes to all five, great, you're in a really strong position. However, if you answered no to
            any of these, it's worth taking a look into. Even if you never talk to us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Grid>
    </section>

    <section id="faqs">
      <Grid>
        <div class="col-span-full lg:col-start-2">
          <h2>FAQs</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Will this cost more than my old agency?</strong> Not necessarily. We'll give you an honest cost estimate
              upfront, no obligation to proceed.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>What happens to my domain and hosting?</strong> That depends on what you currently have access to, working
              that out together is part of the free review.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>How fast can you actually move?</strong> For urgent situations we can usually start within days. For
              a considered switch, at your pace.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Do I need to sign a long contract?</strong> No lock-in contracts.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>My current agency is still around, they're just not delivering, can you still help?</strong> Yes. Plenty
              of people we talk to are in exactly this position, nothing needs to have gone wrong for it to be worth a second
              opinion.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </Grid>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <Grid />
    </section>
  </section>
</Layout>
